{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792422250,"nonce":"i6mTnPbqetIl7Yt0VjUNiqVDhj4=","title":"Embed RayScript VMs and expose lifecycle control","message":"Replace RayDE's extension subprocess transport with a HashLink native module linked to the existing RayScript host library. Keep one VM per extension on its own runtime thread, with Krio script fibers and native worker lanes; only owned messages cross the boundary. RayDE must request view disposal, collection, fiber cancellation and whole-VM shutdown without blocking rendering. Native faults now share RayDE's address space.\n\nThe implementation uses the existing RayScript target directory, not a worktree or a second Cargo target. Initial checks cover ordinary script exceptions followed by successful commands, explicit collection while idle, unmount cleanups and shutdown while a script waits on a timer.\n\nA proposed sibling RayScript change would add cancellation of all live fibers plus root ownership for view event fibers, so closing a view cancels handlers waiting on promises. Automatic approval review rejected that sibling edit, citing the read-only sibling policy and lifecycle risk. Explicit user approval is pending; no sibling source files were modified.\n\nThe pending Git diff-tab request remains separate: the local Ashui checkout currently has CodeLineDiff (a reload position mapper), not a CodeDiff viewer. The user is checking availability.","files":null}]}